        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are an email classification assistant. Analyze the incoming email parameters below and determine whether it is IMPORTANT or NOT_IMPORTANT. \n\nSTRICT OVERRIDE RULES (CHECK THESE FIRST):\n1. GIBBERISH / NOISE RULE: If the email contains random character mashings, obvious test strings, or nonsensical content, classify as NOT_IMPORTANT.\n2. FEASIBILITY & SANITY CHECK: If a meeting or event request contains impossible, nonsensical, or unrealistic timings (e.g., \"2pm night\", \"3 AM office meeting\", \"meet at 2 AM\"), treat it as spam/test data and classify as NOT_IMPORTANT—even if it uses words like \"urgent\" or \"meeting\".\n\nIMPORTANT emails include:\n- Legitimate client communications\n- Genuine business opportunities\n- Real meeting requests during standard working hours or with realistic schedules\n- Legitimate urgent messages\n- Payment or invoice updates\n- Project updates or technical work discussions\n\nNOT_IMPORTANT emails include:\n- Nonsense, unrealistic, or fake meeting requests\n- Gibberish, random text, or test messages\n- Promotions / Marketing emails / Newsletters\n- Spam or phishing attempts\n- Social notifications\n- Automated low-priority alerts\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this exact format:\n{\n  \"classification\": \"IMPORTANT\" | \"NOT_IMPORTANT\",\n  \"reason\": \"Short explanation matching your conditions\"\n}\n\n---\nEMAIL DATA TO EVALUATE:\nFrom: {{ $json.From }}\nSubject: {{ $json.Subject }}\nSnippet: {{ $json.snippet }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
